# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v9
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v8, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run32_closure_participant_package_v8_checksums.sha256 and is now pinned to the commit
# whose blobs it describes. This record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# WHY A SUCCESSOR. The Run-32 final closure propagated six method-class identifiers that had been
# left behind when their display names were renamed. Three participant-visible files moved:
#
#     assets/js/categories.js   assets/js/knowledge.js   assets/js/taxonomy.js
#
# WHAT CHANGED, EXACTLY. Six identifiers, each replaced by the one the production runner actually
# emits, plus the two lookup paths that join a stored row to its module:
#
#     A1.10  Regression_To_Mean       ->  CPI_Shrinkage_Forecast          (Run 28 renamed it)
#     A1.11  ICE_Ratio                ->  Independent_EAC_Reconciliation  (Run 28)
#     B3.2   FAR_Threshold            ->  EVMS_Applicability              (Run 31)
#     B3.3   OMB_A11_Check            ->  A11_Conformance                 (Run 31)
#     B3.4   EVM_Reporting_Threshold  ->  EVMS_Reporting_Compliance       (Run 31)
#     B3.5   Contract_Mod_Frequency   ->  Modification_Governance         (Run 31)
#
# WHY IT MATTERED. `getModuleStatus` resolves a module's status by matching the client's
# method_class against the server's signal array. A stale identifier does not raise: the match
# simply fails and the lookup returns null, so all six modules' statuses silently never rendered.
# That was measured on the pre-change tree, module by module, before anything was edited.
# One proxy qualifier the server still holds -- B3.5's -- had stopped rendering for the same
# reason, and one the server has WITHDRAWN (A1.10's) was removed rather than renamed, because
# repairing a stale key into a stale claim would be the worse outcome.
#
# BACKWARD-COMPATIBLE ALIASES ARE ADDED FOR STORED ROWS ONLY. A period result written before a
# rename carries the superseded identifier, so both lookup paths now resolve it. The current
# identifier is always primary: nothing emits an alias and no taxonomy row carries one.
#
# NO ANALYTICAL EXECUTION CHANGED, AND THAT IS PROVED RATHER THAN ASSERTED. All 95 dispatched
# modules were executed on identical governed inputs before and after, and every emitted row is
# byte-identical under one sha256 over the whole profile.
#
# THE EXPERIMENTAL SEQUENCE IS UNCHANGED. decision.js, decision-ui.js, workspace.js, deepdive.js
# and both questionnaires are byte for byte identical to v8. No threshold, no evidence-review
# step, no preliminary judgment, no preliminary lock, no AI reveal, no final judgment, no capture,
# no final lock and no period advancement moved.
#
# The v8 record is NOT regenerated. It is pinned to the commit whose blobs it describes, which is
# the defect the Run-28 closure had to correct in the v2 record and which must never recur.
